Z||000011||KissMySSFiero||05-30-2001||07:52 PM||||Or is it a Notchback with a Fastback clip?  <BR>Which came first chicken or the egg?<BR>hehe =Þ<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000012||saleenfiero||05-30-2001||08:07 PM||||Don't quote me on this:<BR>Started life as a fastback and won alot of awards in that iteration.  Was converted to a notch type back but as you can still tell, it is not your neighbors notch.  ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Jefrysuko||05-30-2001||08:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KissMySSFiero:<BR><B>Or is it a Notchback with a Fastback clip?  <BR>Which came first chicken or the egg?<BR>hehe =Þ<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>In this case the chicken came first  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>In other words... the car started out it's life as a Black 86 GT (with fastback clip obviously).  Rich chopped the top and retained the fastback look until he developed a crack in the rear clip at the bottom of the sail panels. The next time I saw it after that the clip had been reworked to a notchback and it was purple.  He actually never got to finish it.  Rich became sick and died of cancer so Archie and Paul Vargyas worked together to finish the car.<P>BTW: You guy's did notice the reversed cowl induction and the lip on the trailing edge of the roof.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000014||LT1 Chop Top||05-30-2001||09:13 PM||||I was told that when Archie built the Great Blue Chop Top, Mr. Warber changed his chop top to be different, and to stay a a bit ahead of Archie.......a friendly competition.  I am sure that there were more reasons why Rich changed the look too.....I am told he was quite a perfectionist.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Dave Gunsul||05-30-2001||09:21 PM||||What Jeff wrote above is the real story.<BR>There was a crak and it drove Rich crazy,<BR>he always was a perfectionist.<BR>A buddy of mine painted it, he also painted<BR>Haze's car.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
